.TH "MYD" "1" "July 2025" "myd 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
myd \- vi-like terminal file browser
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmyd\fR [\fIPATH\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBmyd\fR is a terminal user interface (TUI) for browsing and managing the
filesystem. It provides a directory tree with \fBvi\fR-style key bindings,
a live info panel showing file metadata, and proportional size bars that
visualize disk usage at a glance.
.PP
Built with \fBratatui\fR and \fBcrossterm\fR.
.PP
If \fIPATH\fR is provided, the browser starts at that directory. Otherwise,
a directory picker screen is shown with common locations (home, desktop,
downloads, etc.).
.SH KEY BINDINGS
.SS Navigation
.TP
.B j
Move cursor down one line.
.TP
.B k
Move cursor up one line.
.TP
.B h
Collapse the current directory, or move the cursor to the parent entry.
.TP
.B l
Expand the current directory.
.TP
.B gg
Jump to the first line of the tree.
.TP
.B G
Jump to the last line of the tree.
.TP
.B Ctrl+d
Scroll down half a page.
.TP
.B Ctrl+u
Scroll up half a page.
.TP
.B g u
Move cursor to the parent directory.
.TP
.B g d
Prompt for a new root directory and navigate to it.
.TP
.B 0
Collapse all expanded directories.
.TP
.B *
Expand all directories.
.SS File Operations
.TP
.B dd
Delete the currently selected file or directory (with confirmation dialog).
.TP
.B R
Rename the currently selected file or directory.
.TP
.B r
Refresh the file tree and clear the size cache.
.SS View
.TP
.B s
Cycle through sort modes: dirs-first, files-first, largest, smallest.
.TP
.B H
Toggle visibility of hidden (dot) files and directories.
.TP
.B b
Toggle display of proportional size bars in the tree.
.TP
.B /
Search for a file or directory by name.
.TP
.B ? / F1
Show/hide help.
.SS Screen Level
.TP
.B q
Quit the application (or go back to previous directory).
.TP
.B Esc
Quit the application.
.TP
.B Ctrl+r
Refresh the file tree.
.TP
.B Ctrl+b
Toggle the info panel sidebar.
.SH SORT MODES
Press \fBs\fR to cycle through the available sort modes:
.TP
.B dirs-first
Directories are listed before files; alphabetical order within each group.
.TP
.B files-first
Files are listed before directories; alphabetical order within each group.
.TP
.B largest
Items sorted by descending size. Directories are measured recursively.
.TP
.B smallest
Items sorted by ascending size. Directories are measured recursively.
.SH SIZE BARS
Each entry in the tree displays a proportional size bar indicating the item's
share of its parent directory's total content. The bar is color-coded:
.TP
.B Green
The item occupies less than 50% of its parent's total size.
.TP
.B Amber
The item occupies 50\-80% of its parent's total size.
.TP
.B Red
The item occupies more than 80% of its parent's total size.
.PP
Toggle the size bars on and off with \fBb\fR.
.SH INFO PANEL
The right-hand sidebar displays detailed metadata for the currently selected
item:
.TP
.B Name
The file or directory name.
.TP
.B Type
Whether the item is a file or directory.
.TP
.B Size
Human-readable file size (e.g., "245 MB").
.TP
.B Contents
For directories: the count of files and subdirectories.
.TP
.B Permissions
Standard Unix permission string (e.g., \fBdrwxr-xr-x\fR).
.TP
.B Owner / Group
The owning user and group.
.TP
.B Timestamps
Creation, modification, and last access times.
.TP
.B Path
The absolute path to the item.
.PP
Hide or show the panel with \fBCtrl+b\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B myd
Start with the directory picker.
.TP
.B myd ~/Documents
Start browsing at \fB~/Documents\fR.
.TP
.B myd /var/log
Start browsing at \fB/var/log\fR.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
.TP
.B Rust
1.75 or later (stable).
.TP
.B Terminal
A terminal with true color (256-color or 24-bit) support.
.SH INSTALLATION
.PP
.RS
.nf
cargo install \-\-path .
.fi
.RE
.PP
Or run directly without installation:
.PP
.RS
.nf
cargo run
cargo run \-\- ~/Documents
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vi (1),
.BR tree (1),
.BR lf (1)
